There are constants $C,c>0$ with the following property. Let $V$ be a normal projective canonical fourfold with $K_V\sim_{\mathbb Q}0$, and let a finite group $G$ act on $V$. Suppose that every $G$-equivariant rational fibration with geometrically integral generic fibre and with both base and fibre of positive dimension has geometric generic fibre of general type on a smooth projective resolution. It is enough to impose this condition on the rational quotients supplied by Lemma <a href="#lem:generic-chain" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="lem:generic-chain">16</a>. If $P$ is an ample rational Cartier divisor satisfying $g^*P\sim_{\mathbb Q}P$ for every $g\in G$, then $$\label{eq:scalar-bounds}
 \gamma(P;V)\le C(P^4)^{1/4},
 \qquad
 \varepsilon(P;x)\ge c(P^4)^{1/4}$$ at a very general smooth point $x\in V$, where $$\varepsilon(P;x)=
 \inf_{\substack{x\in D\subset V\\D\text{ an integral curve}}}
 \frac{P\cdot D}{\mathop{\mathrm{mult}}_xD}.$$ The constants are independent of $V$, $G$, and $P$.

Let $Z$ be a projective $\mathbb Q$-factorial klt variety, let $\Theta\ge0$ be a rational divisor, and let $S\subset Z$ be an integral subvariety of dimension $d>0$. Suppose that $(Z,\Theta)$ is lc over a neighbourhood of the generic point of $S$, and that $S$ is an lc centre there. For a nef rational Cartier divisor $A$ on $Z$ and a smooth projective resolution $S^*\to S$, one has $$\label{eq:scalar-subadjunction}
 K_{S^*}\cdot(A|_{S^*})^{d-1}
 \le (K_Z+\Theta)|_S\cdot(A|_S)^{d-1}.$$ Here the right-hand side means the intersection of the restricted rational line bundle with the cycle $S$.

Let $Z$ be a projective $\mathbb Q$-factorial klt variety of dimension $n\ge2$, and let $N$ be a big nef semiample rational Cartier divisor. Suppose there are $n+1$ positive rational numbers, with consecutive spacing $\delta>0$, all strictly between $(N^n)^{1/n}$ and $\gamma(N;Z)$. There is a covering family of integral subvarieties $S\subset Z$ of some dimension $0<d<n$ such that, on a smooth projective resolution $S^*$ of its geometric generic member, $$\begin{aligned}
 N^d\cdot S&\le (2/\delta)^{n-d}N^n,
       \label{eq:scalar-track-degree}\\
 K_{S^*}\cdot(N|_{S^*})^{d-1}
 &\le \bigl(K_Z+(2n/\delta)N\bigr)|_S
             \cdot(N|_S)^{d-1}.
       \label{eq:scalar-track-canonical}
\end{aligned}$$

Fix $1\le d\le3$ and a positive rational number $C'$. Let $(W_i,L_i)$ be a sequence of smooth projective $d$-folds with $\kappa(W_i)\ge0$ and big, nef, semiample rational Cartier divisors $L_i$. Suppose that $$\label{eq:scalar-fibre-hypotheses}
 L_i^d\longrightarrow0,
 \qquad K_{W_i}\cdot L_i^{d-1}\le C'L_i^d.$$ After passing to a subsequence and resolving the Iitaka fibrations, their smooth geometric generic fibres $U_i$ have a fixed positive dimension, satisfy $\kappa(U_i)=0$, and obey $$\mathop{\mathrm{vol}}(K_{U_i}+L_i|_{U_i})\longrightarrow0.$$ Here $L_i$ denotes its pullback to the resolved model; its restriction to $U_i$ is big, nef, and semiample. When $\kappa(W_i)=0$, the fibre $U_i$ means $W_i$ itself.
